---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import tools from '../../data/tools-manifest.json';
import retirement from '../../data/tool-retirements.json';
import '../../styles/workshop-directory.css';
const guides = (await getCollection('tools')).filter(entry => !entry.data.draft).sort((a, b) => a.data.title.localeCompare(b.data.title));
const localCount = tools.filter(tool => tool.id !== 'chat-playground').length;
const roles: Record<string, string> = { agents: 'Shape the task', prompts: 'Make and compare', models: 'Plan or try', cost: 'Understand the cost', validation: 'Check the output' };
const behaviour: Record<string, string> = {
  'agent-check': 'Local decision aid · no save',
  'prompt-workbench': 'Local editor · optional browser saves',
  'prompt-diff': 'Local comparison · reads saved versions',
  'json-validator': 'Local schema check · no save',
  'context-window': 'Local plan · dated model limits',
  'model-comparison': 'Local calculation · dated model rates',
  'token-cost': 'Local text estimate · no save',
  'chat-playground': 'OpenRouter request · your key · provider charges',
};
---
<BaseLayout title="Tools" description="Eight inspectable browser tools for prompts, JSON, model costs, context budgets and bounded agent decisions. Start with a worked example.">
  <div class="workshop-directory workshop-shell">
    <header class="directory-hero">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">THE SOFT CAT WORKBENCH</p><h1>Bring a question.<br /><em>Make something useful.</em></h1><p>Edit a prompt, check JSON, plan a context budget or inspect a cost estimate. Small tools with something you can take away.</p><div class="directory-jump"><a class="workshop-button primary" href="#interactive-tools">Find your tool <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/prompts">Browse the prompt recipes ↗</a></div><p class="directory-privacy">{localCount} tools need no API key. Chat Playground is the one that calls a model.</p></div>
      <aside class="directory-first-lap" aria-labelledby="first-lap-heading"><p class="eyebrow">A FIRST LAP / NO ACCOUNT NEEDED</p><h2 id="first-lap-heading">From request<br />to a check.</h2><ol><li><a href="/prompts/data-extraction"><span>01</span><div><strong>Take a worked recipe</strong><p>An invoice with a deliberately missing date.</p></div><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></li><li><a href="/lab/prompt-workbench?recipe=data-extraction"><span>02</span><div><strong>Make it your own</strong><p>Edit the template and inspect the filled messages.</p></div><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></li><li><a href="/lab/json-validator"><span>03</span><div><strong>Check the shape</strong><p>Try a broken JSON example and inspect the errors.</p></div><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></li></ol><p>These steps do not call a model. Schema validation checks structure, not whether an answer is true.</p></aside>
    </header>
    <section class="directory-tools" id="interactive-tools" aria-labelledby="tools-heading"><div class="directory-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">PICK THE JOB</p><h2 id="tools-heading">{tools.length} tools. Each with a purpose.</h2></div><p>No sign-up. Clear inputs. Inspectable outputs.</p></div>
      <div class="directory-tool-grid">{tools.map((tool, index) => <article class={'directory-tool ' + (tool.id === 'chat-playground' ? 'directory-tool-connected' : '')}><div class="directory-tool-meta"><span>{roles[tool.category]}</span><span>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span></div><a href={tool.href}><span class="directory-tool-icon" aria-hidden="true">{tool.icon}</span><h3>{tool.name}</h3><p>{tool.description}</p><span class="directory-tool-open">Open tool <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></span></a><p class="directory-tool-behaviour">{behaviour[tool.id]}</p></article>)}</div>
      <aside class="directory-data-note"><h3>Know what leaves the page.</h3><p>Calculators, editors and validators process your input in the browser. Workbench saves only when you choose. Chat sends your messages and key to OpenRouter when you press Send. The tools show their own dated model records, which are not a promise of live availability.</p><a href="/privacy">Privacy and browser storage ↗</a></aside>
    </section>
    <section class="directory-guides" aria-labelledby="guides-heading"><div class="directory-section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">HOW THE PIECES WORK</p><h2 id="guides-heading">Guides tied to the build.</h2></div></div><div>{guides.map(entry => <a href={'/tools/' + entry.id}><span><h3>{entry.data.title}</h3><p>{entry.data.description}</p></span><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a>)}</div></section>
    <aside class="directory-curation"><p class="eyebrow">THE SHELF CHANGED</p><p>The old {retirement.entries.length}-entry external recommendation series has been retired. The three local guides were corrected against the work. Original dates and source history remain visible.</p><a class="text-link" href="/tools/review">What left, and why ↗</a></aside>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
